eone fulfills their nutritional daily intakes, they are likely to have grown up in a health-conscious childhood home.\n\n4.**If people have good relationships with their parents, then they fulfill their nutritional daily intakes.**\n   - This means that if someone has a good relationship with their parents, they are likely to fulfill their nutritional daily intakes.\n\n5.**If people have good relationships with their parents, then they do not eat salads regularly.**\n   - This suggests that if someone has a good relationship with their parents, they are unlikely to eat salads regularly.\n\n6.**If people visit the gym at least once a day, then they always fulfill their daily nutritional intakes.**If Taylor does not visit the gym at least once a day, it is unlikely that she will meet her daily nutritional requirements.\n\nIt is never the case that Taylor did not grow up in a health-conscious childhood home or does not have a good relationship with her parents, and it is also false that Taylor grew up in a health-conscious childhood home and has a good relationship with her parents.\n\nTherefore, we can deduce that the statement "Taylor visits the gym at least once a day" is **certain** regardless of Taylor\'s upbringing and relationship with her parents.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
