do not develop strong bonds with their family members.**\n   - This indicates that if Luke does not live at home regularly, he would not develop strong bonds with his family members.\n\n5.**If people spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings, then they often did not live at home regularly.**\n   - This means if Luke spends a lot of time with his siblings, he would often not live at home regularly.\n\nGiven these points, we can analyze the situation for Luke:\n\n- Luke either is both a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members, or he neither is a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members.\n\nLet\'s consider each scenario:Luke spends a lot of time hanging out and playing with his siblings based on the given information. Therefore, the statement is certain.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
