messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAll employees who schedule a meeting with their customers will appear in the company today. Everyone who has lunch in the company schedules meetings with their customers. Employees will either have lunch in the company or have lunch at home. If an employee has lunch at home, then he/she is working remotely from home. All employees who are in other countries work remotely from home. No managers work remotely from home. James is either a manager and appears in the company today or neither a manager nor appears in the company today.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? James does not have lunch in the company.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "James does not have lunch in the company" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given information, let\'s break down the problem step by step:.\n\n1.**Identify the key points from the context:**.\n   - All employees who schedule a meeting with their customers will appear in the company today.\n   - Everyone who has lunch in the company schedules meetings with their customers.\n   - Employees will either have lunch in the company or have lunch at home.\n   - If an employee has lunch at home, then he/she is working remotely from home.\n   - All employees who are in other countries work remotely from home.\n   - No managers work remotely from home.\n   - James is either a manager and appears in the company today or neither a manager nor appears in the company today.\n\n2.**Analyze the implications for James:**.\n   - Since James is either a manager and appears in the company today or neither a manager nor appears in the company today, we need to consider both scenarios.\n   - If James is a manager and appears in the company today, then he must have lunch in the company because he schedules meetings with his customers (point 1).\n   - If James is neither a manager nor appears in the company today, then he does not have lunch in the company because he does not schedule meetings with his customers (point 1).\n\n3.**Conclusion:**.Based on the information provided, the correct answer is: True.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
