ently and enjoy the process of cleaning.\n   - If people have parents who are very busy with their regular jobs, then they grew up as only children with no siblings.\n   - All households with a high net income have people who have parents who are very busy with their regular jobs.\n   - Peter is either both a person who spills a lot of food on his clothing and grew up as an only child with no siblings, or he is neither a person who spills a lot of food on his clothing nor grew up as an only child with no siblings.\n\n2.**Analyze the implications:**\n   - Since Peter is either both a person who spills a lot of food on his clothing and grew up as an only child with no siblings, or he is neither a person who spills a lot of food on his clothing nor grew up as an only child with no siblings, we need to consider both scenarios:\n     - **Scenario 1:** Peter spills a lot of food on his clothing and grew up as an only child with no siblings.\n     - **Scenario 2:** Peter does not spill a lot of food on his clothing and did not grow up as an only child with no siblings.\n\n3.**Evaluate each scenario:**\n   - **Scenario 1:** Peter spills a lot of food on his clothing and grew up as an only child with no siblings.\n     - According to the information, if someone spills a lot of food on their clothing, they do not tidy their spaces consistently and enjoy the process of cleaning.\n     - Since Peter spills a lot of food on his clothing, it implies that he does not tidy his spaces consistently and enjoys the process of cleaning.\n     - However, this scenario does not directly relate to whether Peter belongs to a household with a high net income.\n     - Therefore, we cannot conclude that Peter belongs to a household with a high net income based solely on this scenario.According to the information, if someone spills a lot of food on their clothing, they tend to neglect tidying their spaces and dislike the process of cleaning.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
