messages:   84%|########3 | 171/204 [00:31<00:03,  9.44it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nSome basketball players are not American. All basketball players are tall. If someone is tall, they wear large shoes. If someone wears large shoes, they wear large-sized clothes. Yuri does not wear large-size clothes.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? If Yuri is not an American basketball player, then Yuri is a basketball player.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "If Yuri is not an American basketball player, then Yuri is a basketball player" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given information, let\'s break down the problem step by step:.\n\n1.**Given Information:**.\n   - Some basketball players are not American.\n   - All basketball players are tall.\n   - If someone is tall, they wear large shoes.\n   - If someone wears large shoes, they wear large-sized clothes.\n   - Yuri does not wear large-size clothes.\n\n2.**Statement to Evaluate:**.\n   - If Yuri is not an American basketball player, then Yuri is a basketball player.\n\n3.**Reasoning:**.\n   - Let\'s denote:.\n     - \\( A \\): Yuri is an American basketball player.\n     - \\( B \\): Yuri is a basketball player.\n     - \\( T \\): Yuri is tall.\n     - \\( L \\): Yuri wears large shoes.\n     - \\( LS \\): Yuri wears large-sized clothes.\n\n   - From the given information, we have:.\n     - \\( \\neg A \\rightarrow B \\) (Some basketball players are not American, so if Yuri is not an American basketball player, he could still be a basketball player.).\n     - \\( B \\rightarrow T \\) (All basketball players are tall.).\n     - \\( T \\rightarrow L \\) (If someone is tall, they wear large shoes.).\n     - \\( L \\rightarrow LS \\) (If someone wears large shoes, they wear large-sized clothes.).\n     - \\( \\neg LS \\) (Yuri does not wear large-size clothes.).The statement "If Yuri is not an American basketball player, then Yuri is a basketball player" is true.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
